{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build","id":1354595,"title":"[2E] Help with Malfeas Infernal Build","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-12T09:52:15-08:00","id":1354595,"title":"[2E] Help with Malfeas Infernal Build","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hello everyone,</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">we're organizing our Christmas One-shot and we decided to go with Exalted this time. We agreed to go for 2e because we wanted to allow every type of Exalted in the group, which would be very hard to do with 3e. So yeah, we're probably going to end up with a circus of Solars, Abyssals, Infernals and Lunars merrily going around Creation holding hands - doesn't make much sense, but hey, it's a oneshot, who cares <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I decided to go for an Infernal as it's the only type of Exalt I've never personally played. After browsing through the manual I've settled on a sky pirate, Slayer Caste with Malfeas as a Patron. We're all gonna be essence 5, and yes, we are perfectly aware that the rules tend to break down at higher levels of power, but we've been playing Exalted since 2003 so we agreed to avoid building monstrous unhittable perfect defense/soak machines just to keep things interesting.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">So with the combat part already settled (I'm going to pick up a mix and match of Malfeas and Adorjani charms just because I love the visuals of Adorjan) I figured hey, my Patron is like, the Rulers of All Rulers, the King of Kings, the Empyreal Chaos, the very concept of rulership and command, so I should probably pick up a couple Social Charms right? Being a pirate captain also makes sense to be at the very least proficient in leading a crew.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">That's where I stumbled. I scoured through the manual and the only Malfeas social charms I could find were a &quot;perfect defense&quot; against social attacks framed as orders (cool), a related charm that makes YOUR orders become unnatural mental influence (cool) and a pretty convoluted failsafe mechanism where you can mark your followers so if they ever challenge you, you can detonate them on the spot and have everyone who sleeps near the site have horrible nightmares for 10000 years.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">That's it. What am I missing here? Isn't Malfeas supposed to be THE ruler? I get that the Infernal Zenith are more Cecelyne's thing, but I've looked through Cecelyne's charms and they're more about building a cult around you. I don't want a cult. I want do bellow orders at the top of my lungs and have people s**t their pants as they scuttle away trying to please me.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I've never built an infernal before and I've only met them as villains so far so I'm probably missing something very basic here. Can anyone with more experience with 2e infernals give me some pointers?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Thanks in advance!</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10161-aithan","name":"Aithan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T10:11:12-08:00","id":1354601,"title":"","content":"Malfeas' main Social Charm is Green Sun Nimbus Flare <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously, though, it's kinda beyond his understanding that someone could hear his command and not heed it. Those who slight him such don't get the command repeated with more mystical might behind it - they get a lance of radioactive fire in the ass. He's graduated from Darkseid's school of management.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T10:17:38-08:00","id":1354602,"title":"","content":"Yeah actually, speaking with my Storyteller we kinda got to the same conclusion. Malfeas doesn't really have many social charms because the idea of someone not obeying him is alien to him. Guess I'll roleplay him like that then. You disobey me? You must be faulty, time to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10161-aithan","name":"Aithan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T10:25:15-08:00","id":1354603,"title":"","content":"Theion was the the Primordial King.<br /> <br /> Malfeas is Reek.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T10:36:50-08:00","id":1354606,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about it, it's something of a reference to the Old Testament God, in that he doesn't override the free will of his subjects, but scourges the disobedient with fire and brimstone.<br /> <br /> Though Neph preferred to think about him as a teenager with anger management issues.<br /> <br /> Fun fact: Neph once admitted to listening to Linkin Park's <i>Hybrid Theory</i> album when writing Malfeas Charms. If you take a close look at the lyrics of some songs, you can find some pretty direct inspirations.<br /> <br /> Fun fact #2: Malfeas is a living city with a Charm that makes him never fall asleep, and Neph put it in there deliberately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T10:51:22-08:00","id":1354613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354603#post1354603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theion was the the Primordial King.<br /> <br /> Malfeas is Reek.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's really not, though. He's still the King. Sure, he's scarred, beaten and imprisoned, but this only made him angrier. His ambitions are right where they always were, and he will not take shit from anybody just because some cosmic mistake caused him a slight setback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T11:31:47-08:00","id":1354627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354606#post1354606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think about it, it's something of a reference to the Old Testament God, in that he doesn't override the free will of his subjects, but scourges the disobedient with fire and brimstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, Yahweh saves the &quot;overriding free will&quot; thing for when he wants to show off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354606#post1354606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact: Neph once admitted to listening to Linkin Park's <i>Hybrid Theory</i> album when writing Malfeas Charms. If you take a close look at the lyrics of some songs, you can find some pretty direct inspirations.<br /> <br /> Fun fact #2: Malfeas is a living city with a Charm that makes him never fall asleep, and Neph put it in there deliberately.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact #3: HAPEXAMENDIOS from Clive Barker's <i>Imajica</i> is depicted as a massive magnificent living city that destroys other gods out of jealousy and unleashes divine fire on those who anger him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-12-2019, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T11:54:52-08:00","id":1354633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354627#post1354627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, Yahweh saves the &quot;overriding free will&quot; thing for when he wants to show off.</div> </div> </div> </div>For when Malfeas wants to make Passover a thing:<br /> <br /> REMEMBRANCE OF THE TYRANT'S MERCY<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 10m; <b>Mins</b>: Malfeas 0, Essence 4; <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Combo-OK, Emotion, Sorcerous<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Magnanimous Warning Glyph<br /> <br /> For the demons that crawl amid Malfeas\u2019 masochistic continents, surviving a year is cause for celebration. This Charm may be activated at the end of any scene in which the Warlock has caused the deaths of a Magnitude of beings at least equal to his Essence or a being whose Essence rating is at least equal to his own\u2014though he may do so at the head of an army if he desires. All surviving witnesses gain an Intimacy of terrified awe toward the Exalt, and for the next twenty five hours, the Infernal\u2019s effective Cult rating is based on the total number of witnesses (or +1 its usual rating if it would be higher otherwise). So long as survivors remain, his effective Cult rating benefits from this bonus every year on the anniversary of the event. Appropriate countermagic may remove the \u201csurviving witness\u201d status from an individual, or the Infernal may be targeted directly to purge the effects of this Charm entirely.<br /> <br /> With a second purchase at Essence 5+, Exalt may define a number of traditions equal to his Essence that will be used to commemorate his victory. The surviving witnesses intuitively know the proper methods of honoring their tyrant\u2019s mercy. Thereafter, any being who participates in at least half those traditions on the anniversary are regarded as surviving witnesses as well for the purposes of calculating the Infernal\u2019s adjusted Cult rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","user":"Reminiscent Oasis","date":". 12-12-2019, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T11:59:20-08:00","id":1354635,"title":"","content":"So for Malfeas to actually benefit from this Charm he'd have to kill more people than actually exist in a single scene, or an Incarna or one of his fellow Yozis? And if there were a single witness, it'd still boost his Cult rating? And this Intimacy is gained regardless of the resolve of the observers and can't be resisted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-12-2019, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T12:04:23-08:00","id":1354637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354635#post1354635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for Malfeas to actually benefit from this Charm he'd have to kill more people than actually exist in a single scene, or one of his fellow Yozis? And if there were 3,000 witnesses, he'd get a Cult rating of 3,000?</div> </div> </div> </div>Malfeas himself would have upgrades of this Charm, that are more compatible with a being of his magnitude, especially since he'd likely have a base Cult N/A rating anyhow. And if there are 3,000 witnesses, you don't get Cult 3,000, you'd get ... (checks 2e Core Book...) Cult 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T12:07:33-08:00","id":1354639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354637#post1354637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malfeas himself would have upgrades of this Charm, that are more compatible with a being of his magnitude, especially since he'd likely have a base Cult N/A rating anyhow. And if there are 3,000 witnesses, you don't get Cult 3,000, you'd get ... (checks 2e Core Book...) Cult 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, misread that. I've since edited. I'm sleepy, so forgive me please, good night.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T12:16:20-08:00","id":1354642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354639#post1354639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, misread that. I've since edited. I'm sleepy, so forgive me please, good night.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if there were a single witness, it'd still boost his Cult rating? And this Intimacy is gained regardless of the resolve of the observers and can't be resisted? </div> </div> </div>A single surviving witness is a bit iffy, but I'd let it trigger the +1 Cult Bonus (should probably change that to triggering of the effective Cult rating would be <i>equal to</i> or less than the Infernal's actual rating). In that case, it'd just be an inefficient way to get a willpower back later.<br /> <br /> The Intimacy gained follows the default rules of mental influences, though it looks like I forgot to include the Emotion Keyword on this Charm now that I think about it. It costs a single willpower to resist. Its intended to be used a blanket effect against a bunch of extras after you've slain their leaders before their eyes, so they shouldn't wasting their limited willpower to stop the Intimacy. Other PCs, though, they can shrug off this charm easily.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T20:12:34-08:00","id":1354711,"title":"","content":"I always found it odd that Infernals didn't really have a printed &quot;do as I say or pay lots of Willpower&quot; Charm. It seems like a major hole in the Charmset.<br /> <br /> Maybe see if your Storyteller will allow you to make a custom Charm or two? There's no reason that Malfeas shouldn't have something similar to (but much more overt and obvious than) Hypnotic Tongue Technique + Minds Yield to Glory, terrifying his victim into obeying his command.<br /> <br /> An Essence 4+ Slayer should be able to roar &quot;KNEEL BEFORE ME, MORTAL!&quot; in the voice of the King as his glorious infernal crown blazes, and the poor terrified sucker either coughs up 5 WP or drops to his knees so hard they'll bruise.<br /> <br /> Some sort of social attack tricks would fit SWLIHN as well. See here for an example (scroll down to Whispered Name Recruitment): <a href=\"http://www.thefreedomstone.com/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?t=7330\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.thefreedomstone.com/phpBB...pic.php?t=7330</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aithan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354602#post1354602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah actually, speaking with my Storyteller we kinda got to the same conclusion. Malfeas doesn't really have many social charms because the idea of someone not obeying him is alien to him. Guess I'll roleplay him like that then. You disobey me? You must be faulty, time to die.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it's just a wordcount issue, rather than being a deliberate omission that's meant to say something about Malfeas. If Malfeas wasn't supposed to be able to give powerful commands, Crowned With Fury wouldn't be there. (The problem being that Crowned With Fury isn't really that great on its own, although the 2.5 update made it a bit better.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T01:41:26-08:00","id":1354734,"title":"","content":"I would just repurpose a Solar Presence Charm for that purpose. We've done the same thing to make a Medicine Charm tree for Malfeas, with the basic difference being that the Charm only works on the Infernal's own self or her cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T02:44:02-08:00","id":1354737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354711#post1354711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always found it odd that Infernals didn't really have a printed &quot;do as I say or pay lots of Willpower&quot; Charm. It seems like a major hole in the Charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was deliberate. Two things Neph was going for with Infernals were to make them palpably different from other Exalted, and to try and avoid some of the worst aspects of 2e. He was also a strong believer in mechanics encouraging specific behaviors. Some sort of &quot;do as I say or pay lots of WP&quot; was something every other Exalt had in one way or another, and they contributed to social combat being a ridiculous screaming match and mortals being viewed as pawns to be moved about at the whim of Essence-users. Infernal Charms often avoid the social combat system altogether, instead relying on tricking mortals into bargains, forcing servitude upon them against their will rather than bending it, or otherwise going about it in a roundabout way. And of course, they do get to boss lesser demons around. This all helps to make their social interactions more involved, and reinforces their image as demonic warlocks and corrupters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T04:19:30-08:00","id":1354747,"title":"","content":"There are Charms to inflict/create physical mutations. Would Charms that inflict psychological 'mutations' fit? E.g., by making someone more perverse, or more angry, or more vengeful, you can more easily bend them to your will.<br /> <br /> If the Demon City encompasses all, couldn't he encompass others and make them a part of him mentally as well as spiritually? Find the right angle and I think you could shape a Charm around that.<br /> <br /> Thinking of Adorjan for a moment, could her winds scour personalities and flay minds? That might be another route.<br /> <br /> Failing that, you still have your Excellencies to fall back on. There are also Artifacts that might fill the gap?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-13-2019, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T04:53:04-08:00","id":1354751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354711#post1354711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Essence 4+ Slayer should be able to roar &quot;KNEEL BEFORE ME, MORTAL!&quot; in the voice of the King as his glorious infernal crown blazes, and the poor terrified sucker either coughs up 5 WP or drops to his knees so hard they'll bruise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortals kneel before the Slayer not because they can't spend the willpower but because they don't want to be irradiated by Demon Emperor Shintai. If you want a Charm that forces people to prostrate themselves before you as you blaze with infernal glory, I'd rip the environmental damage effect out of Demon Emperor Shintai and make it it's own Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T05:16:07-08:00","id":1354752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354747#post1354747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are Charms to inflict/create physical mutations. Would Charms that inflict psychological 'mutations' fit? E.g., by making someone more perverse, or more angry, or more vengeful, you can more easily bend them to your will.<br /> <br /> If the Demon City encompasses all, couldn't he encompass others and make them a part of him mentally as well as spiritually? Find the right angle and I think you could shape a Charm around that.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as Malfeas is concerned, you're already part of him, because everything that happens is his dream and you're just a tiny part of it. His mind will pay you no more heed than that, and if you act outside the role he envisions for you, he'll just discard you like a broken toy you are. There are billions of insignificant dream-figments like you around, and the Demon City will gladly remove all of them that oppose his will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T06:41:28-08:00","id":1354757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354601#post1354601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malfeas' main Social Charm is Green Sun Nimbus Flare <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously, though, it's kinda beyond his understanding that someone could hear his command and not heed it. Those who slight him such don't get the command repeated with more mystical might behind it - they get a lance of radioactive fire in the ass. He's graduated from Darkseid's school of management.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps that the Malfeas Excellency <b><i>enhances actions isomorphic to being Darkseid, Skeletor or Megatron </i></b>so while you may lack actual unnatural mental influence backing your hate-crazed, hellfire-punctuated rants unless you invest in Crowned With Fury you are absolutely doing the mechanically correct thing by interacting with your minions using as much bombast as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T17:33:05-08:00","id":1354838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354737#post1354737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was deliberate. Two things Neph was going for with Infernals were to make them palpably different from other Exalted, and to try and avoid some of the worst aspects of 2e. He was also a strong believer in mechanics encouraging specific behaviors. Some sort of &quot;do as I say or pay lots of WP&quot; was something every other Exalt had in one way or another, and they contributed to social combat being a ridiculous screaming match and mortals being viewed as pawns to be moved about at the whim of Essence-users. Infernal Charms often avoid the social combat system altogether, instead relying on tricking mortals into bargains, forcing servitude upon them against their will rather than bending it, or otherwise going about it in a roundabout way. And of course, they do get to boss lesser demons around. This all helps to make their social interactions more involved, and reinforces their image as demonic warlocks and corrupters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. I'm honestly not a huge fan of &quot;spend 5 WP or obey!&quot; effects either, but if basically every other Exalt type has them then Infernals definitely should as well. They're already palpably different from other Exalted without forbidding them from such a useful and otherwise-universal type of effect.<br /> <br /> Every Yozi is different and interesting, and that's great (I really do enjoy Cecelyne's wish-granting antics), but the most direct form of persuasion available surely ought to belong to Malfeas -- he isn't much for doing things in roundabout ways. If social combat is a ridiculous screaming match, who can scream louder than the King of Hell? If you <i>don't</i> want social combat to be a ridiculous screaming match, you're probably going to need to take the errata axe to all those other Charmsets. If Infernals can't match anyone else in social combat, they're liable to just attack people instead of talking to them, and that's boring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354751#post1354751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals kneel before the Slayer not because they can't spend the willpower but because they don't want to be irradiated by Demon Emperor Shintai. If you want a Charm that forces people to prostrate themselves before you as you blaze with infernal glory, I'd rip the environmental damage effect out of Demon Emperor Shintai and make it it's own Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the idea of a Malfeas Charm that basically creates an aura of &quot;anyone not obeying my commands takes environmental damage,&quot; but I don't think it should replace the ability to command people to do stuff in a more normal way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T00:20:29-08:00","id":1354860,"title":"","content":"There are these two from Vance:<br /> <br /> Invincible Audacious Narcissism<br /> Cost: \u2013<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Impervious Primacy Mantle<br /> <br /> Malfeas, bound by mutilation of his soul and oaths sworn against his very nature, would shrivel, wither, starve, were it not for his own blind arrogance. So long as he can believe in his own majesty, his own righteousness, the Demon King endures. This Charm grants the Infernal a magical Intimacy to themselves, an Intimacy which cannot be eroded or altered. Any scene that would count as building that Intimacy\u2013the Infernal listened to the obsequious praise of his minions, or writing of his own heroic feats in verse, extolling his prowess to a lover, and so on\u2013allows the Infernal to go a day without need for food or drink, sustained by his own ego. He has no need for mundane nourishment, and suffers no penalty for avoiding it.<br /> <br /> A second purchase at Essence 4 allows the Infernal to renew his mortal flesh as he basks in his ego. Any scene that would count as building his narcissistic Intimacy also either heals the Infernal of a single level of bashing damage, or converts a level of lethal damage to bashing damage. Aggravated damage cannot normally be healed by this Charm, but at Essence 6, the Infernal may convert a level of aggravated damage to lethal damage in any scene that builds his Intimacy.<br /> <br /> Ultimately Bombastic Villainous Monologue<br /> Cost: 5m<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Combo-OK, Compulsion, Social<br /> Duration: (Essence) actions<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Invincible Audacious Narcissism<br /> <br /> Malfeas\u2019s arrogance is not only legendary, but also immanent to his own nature\u2013he is incapable of conceiving of any other being as his equal. He sees all\u2013the Yozis, the gods, the Exalted themselves\u2013as his own personal retinue, to be commanded and threatened. When they will not bow to his will, then let them keep to awe-struck silence! The Infernal rolls (Charisma + Presence) as a social attack against one character, declaiming an arrogant exclamation that brooks no response. If the attack beats the enemy\u2019s highest MDV, then they are shaken by the Infernal\u2019s majesty, and can take only guard actions for the next (Essence) actions. Spending a point of willpower allows them to ignore this compulsion for a single action. However, this over-awing is only effective in social combat\u2013if any character initiates actual combat, the effect of this Charm ends.<br /> <br /> The second one perhaps has some applicability here?<br /> <br /> Source: <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/exalted-malfeas-charms.475226/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...charms.475226/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T11:47:13-08:00","id":1354908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354838#post1354838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it should replace the ability to command people to do stuff in a more normal way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not doing things the &quot;normal way&quot; is the Infernal's whole deal. They're channeling the primordial cosmic forces that forged the universe. Interacting with the world on a mundane human level is challenging for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T21:36:35-08:00","id":1354961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1354595-2e-help-with-malfeas-infernal-build?p=1354908#post1354908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not doing things the &quot;normal way&quot; is the Infernal's whole deal. They're channeling the primordial cosmic forces that forged the universe. Interacting with the world on a mundane human level is challenging for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>My statement was poorly phrased, but while Infernals are certainly characterized by weirdness, not everything they do is totally bizarre, and broadly speaking they do have access to the same types of mechanics that other Exalted do.<br /> <br /> An Infernal who happens to have Crowned With Fury is still giving orders in a basically normal way, he just happens to wear a blazing green crown and be harder to ignore while he does that (and he can't give orders <i>without</i> the effect kicking in, which is the real weird part).<br /> <br /> A straightforward &quot;obey me or pay lots of WP&quot; effect is less interesting than something a bit more unique that reflects the Demon City's nature, but it's still perfectly fitting for his themes. The King gives orders, and his terrified subjects wouldn't dare disobey even if he hasn't actually threatened to irradiate them.<br /> <br /> IMPERIOUS MAJESTY EDICT<br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2014 (4m <i>or</i> 7m <i>or</i> 10m, 1wp); <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Obvious, Social<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Crowned With Fury<br /> <br /> When the King speaks, it is unthinkable that his lessers should fail to obey his wishes. No loyal subject would so much as consider resisting. When the Infernal makes a social attack enhanced by Crowned With Fury against a single target, he may pay four motes to augment the sheer power contained in his voice and bearing; the attack costs two Willpower to resist instead of one, as the very notion of defiance becomes terrifying to the victim. The warlock's burning crown blazes even brighter as he speaks, and his voice seems to echo faintly, like that of Malfeas himself.<br /> <br /> With a second purchase of this Charm, the Infernal may instead spend seven motes while making a social attack enhanced by Crowned With Fury against multiple targets, with the same effect applying to all who hear.<br /> <br /> The third purchase of Imperious Majesty Edict requires Essence 4+, and permits the Infernal to spend ten motes and one Willpower when making a social attack enhanced by Crowned With Fury against a single target in order to increase the cost of resisting his attack to (warlock's Essence, maximum 5) Willpower.<br /> <br /> (Honestly, I'd been thinking of something like this Charm since long before I saw this thread, so I figured I might as well finally write it up. Not 100% sure if the mote costs for the first two effects are appropriate.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}